      "description": "Watch Barnet vs Salford City highlights and goals from League Two on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 15, 2026. The stage was set for a classic League Two encounter at The Hive, with both teams looking to make an early statement in the season. On this afternoon of August 15, 2026 , the atmosphere was thick with anticipation as Barnet welcomed Salford City for a match that would eventually defy all expectations. Salford's First-Half Dominance The contest began with a physical edge, as evidenced by an early booking for Oliver Turton . However, it was the visiting side that found their clinical edge first. In the 24th minute, Salford City broke the deadlock when Oisin Gallagher found the net following a sharp assist from Kabongo Tshimanga . The goal injected confidence into the visitors, who controlled the tempo for much of the opening period. Just before the interval, Salford doubled their lead. In the 42nd minute, Charlie Lakin capitalized on a scoring opportunity to make it 2-0, leaving the home fans stunned. At that stage, Salford City looked firmly in the driver's seat, despite Joe Powell picking up a yellow card in a midfield battle that was becoming increasingly heated. Tactical Adjustments and Rising Tension The second half saw a flurry of tactical changes as both managers looked to influence the outcome. Barnet introduced fresh legs in the form of Daniel Udoh and Brandon Comley , while Salford brought on Jorge Grant and Benjamin Woodburn to shore up the midfield. The match remained a feisty affair, with the referee busy issuing cautions to Luke Molyneux , Zac Williams , and goal-scorer Oisin Gallagher as the game entered its final quarter. Stoppage Time Heroics With only minutes remaining on the clock, the script was completely rewritten. In the 87th minute, Kabongo Tshimanga turned from provider to finisher, pulling one back for Barnet after being set up by Nnamdi Ofoborh . The goal transformed the energy within the stadium, sparking a relentless late charge from the hosts. As the match entered the 90th minute, the unthinkable happened. Adebola Oluwo met a cross from Joe Powell to hammer home the equalizer, completing a stunning comeback in the space of just three minutes. After a tense eight minutes of stoppage time, the final whistle blew on a 2-2 draw, leaving Barnet celebrating a hard-earned point and Salford City wondering how they let a two-goal lead slip away."
